{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792402589,"nonce":"Ei+rHyk84DBoYQeiwVGaClkq2PI=","title":"The nightly release fails at its web build step: Haxe reports \"Multiple targets\"","message":"**What happens**\n\nThe release workflow's job \"package and validate Haxelibs\" has failed since 2026-10-18 (scheduled runs 39111025709 and 39229050696) at the step \"Compile a web build and check that the page's library is staged\", with `Error: Multiple targets`. publish release is skipped after it, so no nightly is published.\n\n**Cause**\n\ntests/fixtures/package/build.hxml names its own target (`-hl tests/bin/package-consumer.hl`), and that step adds a second, `-hl tests/bin/web/package-consumer.hl`. Haxe 4.3.6 refuses two targets (checked with a two-line hxml). The step arrived with 6f496f1 and 35e647a.\n\n**Fix**\n\nThe target comes off the build file and each caller gives its own: the native steps of ci.yml and release.yml `-hl tests/bin/package-consumer.hl`, the web step the web one. A release run with no tag (validate only) checks it.","files":null}]}